From 99b8710fdf17cec933c27b2d0128520556481df8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 09:59:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 274/280] WIP: drm/rockchip: vop: reject AFBC with a virtual
 width

The VOP AFBC decoder is programmed with the source size only and cannot
skip a stride wider than the source, so a cropped AFBC buffer is scanned
out with the wrong layout.

Reject AFBC planes whose source width differs from the framebuffer
width, as the vendor kernel does on RK3399.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop.c
index 74d5a8dc2675..3966f241c010 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop.c
@@ -928,6 +928,12 @@ static int vop_plane_atomic_check(struct drm_plane *plane,
 				      new_plane_state->rotation);
 			return -EINVAL;
 		}
+
+		if (fb->width != drm_rect_width(&new_plane_state->src) >> 16) {
+			DRM_DEBUG_KMS("AFBC does not support a virtual width, fb width=%u\n",
+				      fb->width);
+			return -EINVAL;
+		}
 	}
 
 	return 0;
-- 
